<title>MALDIVES: India, Pakistan leaders agree prisoner release.</title>
<headline>India, Pakistan leaders agree prisoner release.</headline>
<dateline>KURUMBA, Maldives 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The leaders of India and Pakistan said they had agreed in their first talks for four years on Monday to release all prisoners from each others' countries.</p>
<p>Indian Prime Minister Inder Kumar Gujral and his Pakistani counterpart, Nawaz Sharif, said they also agreed during a 90-minute meeting to establish a telephone hotline.</p>
